  "term": "noncompliance",
  "definition": "In this context, noncompliance means not starting, tolerating, or completing the recommended elements of treatment, such as enough exposure and response prevention practice between sessions. The source also notes that what is labeled noncompliance may often reflect limited capacity to carry out treatment rather than simple unwillingness.",
